Hi! I found that the constructor might be missing in py-binding/control/planners/sst .

`    planner = planners[planner_name](si)
              ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
TypeError: ompl._ompl.control.SST: no constructor defined!
`

The source file (https://github.com/ompl/ompl/blob/main/py-bindings/control/planners/sst/SST.cpp) looks like this, which does not have the lines for constructor:

`#include <nanobind/nanobind.h>
#include "ompl/control/planners/sst/SST.h"
#include "../../init.h"

namespace nb = nanobind;
namespace oc = ompl::control;
namespace ob = ompl::base;

void ompl::binding::control::initPlannersSst_SST(nb::module_ &m)
{
    nb::class_<oc::SST, ob::Planner>(m, "SST");
}`

When I downloaded the source file and added the lines found in (https://github.com/ompl/ompl/blob/main/py-bindings/control/planners/rrt/RRT.cpp) but swapped RRT for SST, it resolved the issue. 

I wonder if it is a bug and if this is the correct way to use it for now.

Thanks for your assistance!
